Privacy Policy

Privacy Policy

Last updated: July 2026

Introduction

RotaRight ("we", "our", or "us") provides employee scheduling, payroll and workforce management services.

This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it and your rights regarding your personal data.

Information We Collect

Depending on how your employer uses RotaRight, we may collect:

Personal information
Name
Email address
Phone number
Job role
Employment information
Assigned locations
Groups or departments
Shift schedules
Availability
Leave requests
Shift swaps
Payroll information
Clock in/out history
Bank details

Where payroll features are used we may store:

Account holder name
Bank name
Sort code
Account number

These details are encrypted and only accessible to authorised managers and administrators within your organisation.

Emergency contact information

Your employer may store:

Emergency contact name
Phone number
Location data

If your employer enables location verification, RotaRight records your location only when you clock in or clock out.

RotaRight does not continuously track your location and does not access location data in the background.

Technical information

We may automatically collect:

Device type
Operating system
App version
Crash reports
Diagnostic information
Push notification token (if notifications are enabled)
How We Use Your Information

We use your information to:

Manage employee schedules
Record attendance
Process payroll
Verify clock in/out location (if enabled)
Send work-related notifications
Improve app performance
Maintain security
Sharing Information

We do not sell your personal information.

Your information may be shared only with:

Your employer
Authorised managers within your organisation
Trusted service providers (such as Supabase for secure data storage)
Legal authorities where required by law
Data Security

We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information against unauthorised access, disclosure or loss.

Sensitive information such as bank details is stored securely and access is restricted to authorised users.

Data Retention

Your information is retained while your employer maintains your account and for any period required to comply with legal or payroll obligations.

Your Rights

Depending on your location, you may have rights to:

Access your personal data
Correct inaccurate information
Request deletion of your account
Request a copy of your information

Requests should normally be made through your employer, who controls your organisation's data.

Account Deletion

You may request deletion of your RotaRight account at any time.

How to request deletion

Contact your organisation's administrator or email:

Please include:

Your name
Email address
Organisation name
What will be deleted

When your account is deleted we will remove:

Login credentials
Personal profile information
Contact information
Emergency contact details
Bank details
Device tokens
What may be retained

Some information may be retained where required by law or legitimate business purposes, including:

Payroll records
Clock in/out history
Shift records
Audit logs

These records are retained only where legally required or necessary for employment record keeping.

